  "title": "osf review: multi-agent PR review pipeline",
  "summary": "Adds a full review subsystem to osf: a lens catalogue (20 shipped lenses plus repository overrides), a reviewer roster resolved from `[agents]` in osf.toml, per-reviewer headless runs in a clean copy of the change, quote verification of every finding against the real files, a deterministic reducer that turns answers into a verdict, and a GitHub Actions workflow that builds osf from the base branch, runs each reviewer in its own job with only its own provider key, and posts the decision. It also reworks suppression markers so a marker is only judged unused by the checker that owns its rules, and adds `--no-suppress` for CI.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
